A tube is open at both ends. A loudspeaker, emitting sound of a single frequency, is placed near one end of the tube, as shown in Fig. 3.1.
{{figure:figure_3_1.png}}
The speed of the sound in the tube is 340 m s⁻¹. The length of the tube is 0.60 m. A stationary wave is formed with an antinode A at each end of the tube and two antinodes inside the tube.
